Nivel de vechime: Nivel mediu de experiență
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Securitatea computerelor și a rețelelor
REVELSI is a global cybersecurity, AI, software, and infrastructure services organization. We work with worldwide enterprises to design, build, secure, and operate the systems their business depends on. Our top priority is safeguarding the fast-evolving global infrastructures and technologies. We integrate cybersecurity into infrastructure development and operational processes, alongside software development, to proactively stay at the leading edge of industry
 advancements.
 REVELSI TEAM 
 At REVELSI, we combine deep technical expertise with a Silicon Valley-inspired mindset: agile, innovative, and collaborative. We’re a collaborative team that values performance and a positive work environment. We are committed to delivering high-quality results, supporting each other, and fostering a professional and friendly atmosphere. We’re looking for a team player with specialized skills and ready to make an impact alongside experts in cybersecurity, network design, architecture, AI & software development, and IT management. You’ll collaborate with experienced IT (Security) professionals, expand your skills, and enjoy the journey in a team that embraces challenges with energy and enthusiasm.
 YOUR DAY TO DAY: 
Design and implement security architectures for networks, systems, and applications, integrating security-by-design principles from the earliest stages;
Deploy, configure, and operate network security solutions (next-generation firewalls, IDS/IPS, VPN/IPsec, NAC, web and email filtering), keeping them running at peak performance;
Design and secure inter-site and multi-cloud connectivity (IPsec, SD-WAN) and implement cloud network security controls: segmentation, security groups, private connectivity, and Zero Trust architectures (Azure, AWS, GCP);
Secure container and Kubernetes networking (network policies, ingress, service exposure), including for AI infrastructure hosted in client environments;
Run vulnerability assessments on network infrastructure, prioritize risks, and coordinate remediation and patching for network devices;
Monitor network security events, respond promptly to alerts, and support incident investigations with root cause analysis;
Manage identity and privileged access to network infrastructure (IAM, PAM/PIM, just-in-time access);
Define and maintain network security standards, policies, and documentation aligned with ISO 27001, NIST, and CIS Controls;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams (SOC, AI, cloud, software development) and support client engagements: assessments, security reviews, and technical workshops.
 YOUR PROFILE: 
Bachelor’s degree in computer science, telecommunications, or a related field;
3+ years of hands-on experience in network security engineering roles;
Strong knowledge of networking protocols and technologies (TCP/IP, routing, switching, DNS, TLS);
Hands-on experience with firewalls and network security solutions (e.g. Fortinet, Palo Alto, Cisco), IDS/IPS, and VPN/IPsec;
Experience securing cloud networks (Azure, AWS, or GCP): segmentation, security groups, private connectivity;
Scripting languages (Python, PowerShell) and infrastructure-as-code tools (Terraform);
Knowledge of security standards and regulations (ISO 27001, NIST, GDPR, HIPAA);
Strong problem-solving and communication skills.
Network security certifications: CCNP Security, PCNSE, Fortinet NSE 4+, Microsoft AZ-700/AZ-500, or CISSP (considered a plus);
Experience with SD-WAN, Zero Trust network architectures, and NAC solutions (considered a plus);
Kubernetes and container networking security experience (considered a plus);
Experience in an MSSP or client-facing environment (considered a plus);
Willing to work from Monday to Friday between 12:00 and 21:00 with 1 hour lunch break, in a hybrid system (4 days from our office).
 WE VALUE OUR EMPLOYEES: 
 At REVELSI, we create an environment that supports your well-being, growth, and work-life balance:
Private healthcare & medical insurance
Private dental services
Meal vouchers
Referral bonus program
Learning & development opportunities
Team buildings & events
Pizza day and free drinks at the office
Seasonal gifts (Christmas / Easter)
21 days PTO, increasing up to 25 based on seniority
 Ready to Join Us?
 Click “Apply” and let’s get started!
 Every day is an opportunity to grow and go beyond our limits! We embrace challenges and succeed together as a team—because great things happen when we collaborate.
